    {
      "id": "s06",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "transition": "wipe",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Start with the idea that changes how you read every line of Playwright code.",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {
          "number": "01",
          "title": "A locator is a saved search",
          "subtitle": "Not the element itself"
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 150,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-04-locators_long_s06.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "type": "CODE_WINDOW",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Two lines. The first one names the button, and it searches nothing at all. Nothing happens on that page. All you have done is write a description down: the button that says Sign in. The search only runs on the second line, at the moment you click.",
      "data": {
        "code": {
          "filename": "locator.py",
          "language": "py",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "# A locator is a SAVED SEARCH, not the element",
              "color": "green"
            },
            {
              "text": "sign_in = page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Sign in\")"
            },
            {
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "text": "# Nothing searched yet. It runs when you ACT:",
              "color": "green"
            },
            {
              "text": "sign_in.click()",
              "color": "purple"
            }
          ],
          "atWord": 10.583
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 436,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-04-locators_long_s07.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s08",
      "type": "KINETIC_TEXT",
      "transition": "glitch",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "So a locator is not the element. It is a saved search for the element, and Playwright holds that search back until the very last moment, then goes and looks fresh.",
      "data": {
        "kinetic": {
          "text": "Nothing has searched yet.",
          "fx": "typewriter",
          "sub": "the search runs when you act",
          "atWord": 9.083
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 321,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-04-locators_long_s08.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s09",
      "type": "SPLIT_PATHS",
      "transition": "morph",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Which matters more than it sounds. Say the button turns up two seconds late, because part of the page is still loading. The old style grabs the element the second you ask, so it grabs nothing and falls over. A locator looks again when you click.",
      "data": {
        "center": {
          "kicker": "the button arrives 2s late",
          "title": "Same page, two ways",
          "atWord": 7.25
        },
