    {
      "id": "s13",
      "type": "CODE_DIFF",
      "transition": "dip",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Here is a thing developers do every other Tuesday. They restyle a page, and the class names all change. Nothing a user can see is any different. But if your script was pointing at that old class name, every test you wrote just went red.",
      "data": {
        "diff": {
          "fileName": "login.html",
          "stat": {
            "plus": 1,
            "minus": 1
          },
          "atWord": 12.917,
          "rows": [
            {
              "kind": "ctx",
              "text": "<form class=\"login\">"
            },
            {
              "kind": "del",
              "text": "  <button class=\"btn-primary-2xl\">Sign in</button>"
            },
            {
              "kind": "add",
              "text": "  <button class=\"ui-btn-v3\">Sign in</button>"
            },
            {
              "kind": "ctx",
              "text": "</form>"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 450,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-04-locators_long_s13.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "type": "DOM_INSPECT",
      "transition": "zoom",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "That is because a class name describes how the page was built. The nesting, the position, the styling. All of that belongs to the developers and they change it whenever they like. It says nothing about what the button means.",
      "data": {
        "dom": {
          "selector": "form > div > .btn-primary-2xl",
          "nodes": [
            {
              "tag": "form",
              "attr": "class=\"login\"",
              "depth": 0
            },
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attr": "class=\"row\"",
              "depth": 1
            },
            {
              "tag": "button",
              "attr": ".btn-primary-2xl",
              "depth": 2
            },
            {
              "tag": "span",
              "attr": "Sign in",
              "depth": 3
            }
          ],
          "highlight": 2,
          "atWord": 9.333
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 384,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-04-locators_long_s14.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "type": "CODE_WINDOW",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "So describe it the way a person would. Nobody says click the div with class b t n dash primary. They say click the Sign in button. That is all get by role does. A role, and the name the user can actually read.",
      "data": {
        "code": {
          "filename": "roles.py",
          "language": "py",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Sign in\").click()",
              "color": "green"
            },
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_role(\"link\", name=\"Pricing\").click()"
            },
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_role(\"heading\", name=\"Welcome back\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_role(\"checkbox\","
            },
            {
              "text": "                 name=\"Remember me\").check()"
            },
            {
              "text": "email = page.get_by_role(\"textbox\", name=\"Email\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "email.fill(\"neo@matrix.io\")"
            }
          ],
          "atWord": 14.25
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 432,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-04-locators_long_s15.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "transition": "wipe",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Roles cover most of a page. Forms need a couple of extra friends.",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {
          "number": "03",
          "title": "The rest of the family",
          "subtitle": "Label, placeholder, text, test id"
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 153,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-04-locators_long_s16.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "type": "WINDOW_FRAME",
      "transition": "slide",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Look at a real form. Every box has a label sitting beside it, and that label is how your eyes know which box is which. Get by label uses the very same thing, and it is the way you fill in forms.",
      "data": {
        "window": {
          "variant": "browser",
          "url": "shop.example.com/login",
          "title": "Sign in",
          "content": {
            "kind": "form",
            "title": "Sign in",
            "fields": [
              {
                "label": "Email",
                "value": "neo@matrix.io"
              },
              {
                "label": "Password",
                "value": "",
                "focus": true
              }
            ],
            "submit": "Sign in"
          },
          "atWord": 10.417
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 359,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-04-locators_long_s17.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s18",
      "type": "CODE_WINDOW",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "And the rest, one line each. Placeholder, for grey hint text in an empty box. Text, for a message on the page. Test id, for an attribute added only for tests, the sturdiest of the lot. And alt text, for images.",
      "data": {
        "code": {
          "filename": "family.py",
          "language": "py",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_label(\"Email\").fill(\"neo@matrix.io\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "box = page.get_by_placeholder(\"Search docs...\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "box.fill(\"locators\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_text(\"Thanks for signing up!\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_test_id(\"checkout-btn\").click()",
              "color": "green"
            },
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_alt_text(\"Company logo\")"
            }
          ],
          "atWord": 11
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 470,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-04-locators_long_s18.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "type": "QUIZ_CARD",
      "transition": "iris",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Second check. You need to fill the box underneath the label Password. Which of these four do you reach for? Have a think, and pause the video if you want longer. Ready? B again. Get by label joins a label to its box.",
      "data": {
        "quiz": {
